 {"id": "DOC-5", "title": "[P4] docs/INSTALL.md:116-147 pastes a `lore --help` block the binary has never printed — the gate and audit entries carry two clauses that exist in no revision of lore/__main__.py", "status": "complete", "priority": "P4", "created_by": null, "reasoning": "DOC SEVERITY P4 by Bane's 2026-09-30 ruling: documentation findings file at P4 (P5 for polish only), never P1-P3, and a doc row must never outrank a functional defect in the foreman's pick order. Nothing here destroys data, so no P1. Do not re-raise this at a higher priority.\n\nGAP: docs/INSTALL.md pastes a `lore --help` block that the binary has never printed. Two entries in the pasted block carry clauses that exist in NO revision of lore/__main__.py.\n\nThe doc's own promises (both falsified):\n- docs/INSTALL.md:3-4 — \"Everything here was run and its output pasted verbatim.\"\n- docs/INSTALL.md:109 — section heading \"### `--help` — the whole shipped surface\"; the fenced block that claims to be the command's output runs docs/INSTALL.md:116-147.\n\nEXECUTED at HEAD f83e7bff (2026-10-19), from the repo root:\n  uv run python -m lore --help\nand diffed programmatically against the fenced block (script: /home/kara/.hermes/stand-in/docs/lore/help_diff.py; diff: /home/kara/.hermes/stand-in/docs/lore/help-diff.txt). Two hunks differ, both extra text in the DOC:\n\n  (a) docs/INSTALL.md:132-134 (gate entry) pastes:\n        \"... exit 0 = allowed, 1 = denied; opt-in --record PATH appends one\n         JSONL audit record per ALLOWED verdict (denials never write)\"\n      the live binary prints only:\n        \"... exit 0 = allowed, 1 = denied\"\n\n  (b) docs/INSTALL.md:142-144 (audit entry) pastes:\n        \"... never fabricated dates; the `unclassified` catch-all bucket is marked\n         (`bucket: true` in JSON, `[bucket]` prefix in table) so it never reads as\n         a 14th class\"\n      the live binary prints only:\n        \"... never fabricated dates\"\n\nDISCRIMINATING COMMANDS (this is not \"drift\", this text was never the binary's output):\n  grep -rn \"opt-in --record PATH appends\" lore/            -> no match at HEAD\n  git log --oneline -S\"opt-in --record PATH appends\" -- lore/__main__.py   -> EMPTY (no revision ever contained it)\n  grep -rn \"catch-all bucket is marked\" lore/              -> no match at HEAD\n  git log --oneline -S\"catch-all bucket is marked\" -- lore/__main__.py     -> EMPTY\nSo INSTALL's block was hand-edited; a reader who runs the documented command and diffs sees a doc/binary mismatch and reasonably suspects their install.\n\nFACTS BEHIND THE INSERTED TEXT ARE REAL — keep them, move them out of the fence:\n- `--record` is a real, shipped flag; its own help lives in `lore gate --help` (lore/__main__.py:862 \"REVIEW-LORE-001 OPT-IN: append one durable JSONL audit record\") and in prose at README.md:245-248 and docs/INSTALL.md:384-390.\n- The bucket marker is real for the table and json renderers; the md renderer gap is ALREADY OWNED by pending row README-3 — do not re-handle it here.\n\nFIX (one sitting, docs/INSTALL.md only):\n1. Re-paste the true `uv run python -m lore --help` output verbatim into the fence at docs/INSTALL.md:116-147 (the eight-verb list is unchanged and correct).\n2. If the --record / bucket detail is worth keeping in that section, put it as prose BELOW the fence (reuse the existing README.md:245-248 and README.md:395-403 wording) — never inside a block presented as command output.\n\nACCEPTANCE (reviewer's falsifiable test): `uv run python -m lore --help` writes to a file and `diff` against the fenced block in docs/INSTALL.md is EMPTY; and no sentence inside that fence is absent from the binary's own output (checked by the same diff).\n\nch:trace row=DOC-5 spec=docs/INSTALL.md#the-help-the-whole-shipped-surface test=none:no-test-covers-pasted-help-fidelity doc=docs/INSTALL.md#L116 evidence=/home/kara/.hermes/stand-in/docs/lore/audit-lore-docs-2026-10-19-21-37-57.md witness=none:cli-help-ou